        <p class="profile-detail-region">Movement · Sub-Saharan Africa</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Pan-Africanism</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">Arose among people of African descent in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>; spread to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> and then across the continent</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">From the Pan-African Conference in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1900 to the present: congresses in 1900–1945, independence from 1957, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/organisation-of-african-unity">Organisation of African Unity</a> from 1963 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-union">African Union</a> from 2002</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Leading figures</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-sylvester-williams">Henry Sylvester Williams</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-e-b-du-bois">W. E. B. Du Bois</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marcus-garvey">Marcus Garvey</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-padmore">George Padmore</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kwame-nkrumah">Kwame Nkrumah</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-nyerere">Julius Nyerere</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">Inspired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>’s independence movements and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/organisation-of-african-unity">Organisation of African Unity</a>, succeeded by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/african-union">African Union</a>; continental political union was never achieved</span></div>
        </div>
